WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.000
-The GOP is facing blowback

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.300
for heckling President Biden

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.267
during his state of the union
address last night

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:08.934
after he accurately pointed out
that several Republicans

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.968
had proposed cutting
Social Security and Medicare.

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:12.601
Meanwhile,
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:14.133
stood up and shouted
in a fur coat,

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.234
like a Real Housewife

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:16.968
who wasn't allowed
into a reunion show.

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:18.868
[ Laughter ]
But, other than that,

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:20.501
Republicans had
a pretty great night.

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:22.501
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:26.334
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.501
You might remember that,
after Donald Trump's

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:30.934
rogues' gallery
of dip[bleep] and doofuses

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.601
[ Laughter ]
got creamed in the
midterm elections,

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:35.467
the big takeaway for Republicans
was just be normal.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.267
[ Laughter ]
That was basically

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:40.701
their "Clear eyes, full heart,
can't lose."

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:43.067
[ Laughter ]
Trump and his MAGA allies
in the GOP

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:45.400
handpicked a bunch
of ostentatious weirdos,

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.467
like vampire enthusiast
Herschel Walker;

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:49.667
[ Laughter ]
Pixar villain Kari Lake;

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:52.234
and Area 51 escapee Dr. Oz,

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:54.033
[ Laughter ]
who campaigned --

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:55.267
campaigned for Senate
in Pennsylvania

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:56.968
by wandering
down the produce aisle,

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:59.067
complaining
about the price of crudité

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:01.334
at a grocery store he called
Wegners,

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.934
which does not exist.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:05.334
Of course, the weirdest part
of that video

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:08.701
was always the fact that he
grabbed salsa for a crudité.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.567
Who puts salsa in their crudité?

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.534
[ Laughter ]
He's like a college sophomore

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.334
putting out hors d'oeuvres
for a date.

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.234
[ Baritone ]
Would you like some Funyuns
with your crudité?

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:18.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:19.667
Perhaps some Franzia.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.734
I have a January Chardonnay.

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:22.934
That's a very good month.

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:25.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:26.901
So, after those candidates lost,

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.167
Republicans spent
the next few days

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:30.434
lamenting how weird their party
had gotten

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:33.400
and pleading for Republicans
to just be normal again.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.667
-The Republican Party needs
to do

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:38.634
a really deep introspection look
in the mirror right now,

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:41.367
because this is --
this is an absolute disaster

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.200
for the Republican Party.

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:55.701
[ Laughter ]
-We've attracted these
more cartoon characters

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:57.634
and, if somebody speaking
at a rally

00:01:57.634 --> 00:01:59.934
with a president
or a presidential candidate

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:01.834
is best known
as a pillow salesman,

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:03.067
[ Laughter ]
run to high heaven.

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:06.133
-Okay, but if that pillow
salesman is Mike Lindell,

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.667
it doesn't matter
how far you run --

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.801
you will never be out of range
for his voice.

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:11.968
[ Laughter ]
True story -- they say,
if you listen closely,

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:15.167
you can even hear Mike Lindell
screaming about voting machines

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:17.734
when you hold a seashell
up to your ear.

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:20.334
[ Laughter ]
Watch. [Indistinct]

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:23.067
-Get one machine, open it up,
and look in there.

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:26.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:27.000
[ Clap ]

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.033
-[ Stage whisper ]
You did -- You did great!

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:33.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.934 --> 00:02:36.133
Arguably, the first big test
of whether Republicans

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.300
could prove they were
a normal governing party was

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.734
in the speakership vote
in January,

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:42.100
a test they failed miserably,
after it took 15 rounds

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.200
to elect Kevin McCarthy
as their new speaker

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.601
and one of their members tried
to physically assault

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:48.367
another one on the House floor,

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:51.200
leaving this infamous photo
of a Republican congressman

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.400
being restrained by his face,

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.934
so that he couldn't
punch out a colleague.

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:56.834
He looked like he just got
to a house party

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:59.000
and found out there was salsa
in the crudité.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.567
"That's an affront to God,
you son of a bitch!"

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.567
So, Republicans
failed that test,

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:07.200
but they had a second chance
to make things right

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.067
during President Biden's state
of the union address.

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:13.400
All they had to do was sit there
and listen and not be insane.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.968
Just be normal!

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:16.601
[ Laughter ]
Unfortunately,
it seems like some of them

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:18.167
skipped their
electroshock therapy

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:19.534
[ Laughter ]
because they spent
the night heckling

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:21.400
and yelling incoherently
from the back rows,

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.767
like Marjorie Taylor Greene,
who was seen screaming

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.634
and pointing fingers
in a white fur coat,

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:28.200
like a Long Island dance mom
about to get her final warning.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:32.400
"Ma'am, how many times do we
have to tell you to sit down?"

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.601
[ New York accent ]
How many times do I have
to tell my Kaylie

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:36.601
to get your goshdarn
steps right?!

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:38.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:39.634
Why is she wearing
a white fur coat

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:40.868
to the state of the union
address?

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:43.667
She looks like
an old rapper's first wife.

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:45.501
[ Laughter and oohs ]

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:47.968
With that said, it probably
should not have shocked us

00:03:47.968 --> 00:03:49.267
that Greene decided to act

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:51.334
like an obnoxious weirdo
at the state of the union,

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:53.467
given that, just a few hours
before the speech,

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.934
she posted a video of herself
walking the halls of Congress

00:03:55.934 --> 00:03:58.033
while holding
a single white balloon,

00:03:58.033 --> 00:03:59.734
in what I'm guessing
was supposed to be

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:01.968
some sort of statement
about Joe Biden's handling

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:03.701
of the suspected
Chinese spy balloon.

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:04.767
[ Laughter ]
I mean, look at her.

00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:06.334
She looks like she threw herself

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.701
a Sweet 16 party
and no one showed up.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:10.801
[ Laughter ]
[ As Greene ]
Maybe everybody went

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:12.334
to the other Shakey's.

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:13.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:14.934
Now, Biden did give them plenty

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:16.334
of opportunities to be normal.

00:04:16.334 --> 00:04:17.934
He ticked through a series
of what should've been

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:19.434
bipartisan applause lines,

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:21.400
but the new Republican speaker
of the House, Kevin McCarthy,

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.400
sitting behind Biden
for the first time,

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:26.067
made a show of refusing
to stand or applaud.

00:04:26.067 --> 00:04:28.167
In fact, McCarthy couldn't
even bring himself to applaud

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.634
when Biden simply condemned
the January 6th insurrection

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.667
and said nice things
about democracy.

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:35.033
-Two years ago, democracy faced
its greatest threat

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:37.901
since the Civil War and today,
though bruised,

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:41.067
our democracy remains
unbowed and unbroken.

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:44.968
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:46.267
[ Laughter ]
-That's the face of a guy

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:48.701
who knows that, every time
he claps for Joe Biden,

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:52.033
his phone call from Donald Trump
gets 11 minutes longer.

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:53.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:56.734
And, somehow, the ring gets
louder when he calls, too?

00:04:56.734 --> 00:04:57.400
[ Nokia ringtone ]

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.300
Oh!
[Bleep]

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.567
[ Laughter ]
[ As McCarthy] Hello, Mr. Trump.

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:02.067
How does he change my ringtone?

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.601
You know what? Let me switch
back to my other phone.

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:09.467
-Get one machine, open it up,
and look in there.

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:11.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:13.667
-[ Stage whisper ] I knew
calling you back was a mistake,

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:15.033
but I couldn't change
the script.

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:18.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:19.601
It was too --
I thought, the first time,

00:05:19.601 --> 00:05:21.567
you'd do better and we'd call it
back, but then --

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:22.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:25.033
I couldn't signal them to --

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.767
So, anyway, it was fine.
You did great both times.

00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:29.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:33.834
No, we won't be --

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:35.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:37.100
[ Laughter fades ]
We won't be needing you
tomorrow.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:46.267
[ Cheering ]

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:50.868
[ Thudding ]
[ Laughter and ohhs ]

00:05:50.868 --> 00:05:52.133
Now, Biden definitely took --

00:05:52.133 --> 00:05:53.634
There's no one in there.

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:55.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.901 --> 00:05:59.200
[ Mouthing "There was" ]

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.467
Now, Biden definitely took some
digs at Republicans, to be sure,

00:06:03.467 --> 00:06:05.634
like when he touted his
bipartisan infrastructure bill

00:06:05.634 --> 00:06:07.667
and said he'd even fund projects

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:09.901
in districts where Republican
members of Congress voted

00:06:09.901 --> 00:06:11.133
against the bill.

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:13.067
-I want to thank
my Republican friends

00:06:13.067 --> 00:06:15.033
who voted for the law

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:18.634
and my Republican friends
who voted against it as well.

00:06:18.634 --> 00:06:21.634
But I'm still -- I still get
asked to fund the projects

00:06:21.634 --> 00:06:23.467
in those districts as well,
but don't worry.

00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:25.367
[ Laughter ]
I promised I'd be a president

00:06:25.367 --> 00:06:26.934
for all Americans.
-Whoo!

00:06:26.934 --> 00:06:28.767
[ Applause ]
-We'll fund these projects

00:06:28.767 --> 00:06:30.634
and I'll see you
at the groundbreaking!

00:06:31.901 --> 00:06:34.133
[ Laughter ]
-That's a very, very Biden line.

00:06:34.133 --> 00:06:36.367
"I'll see you
at the groundbreaking."

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:38.167
[ As Biden ]
I'll shake your hand,
kiss your baby,

00:06:38.167 --> 00:06:40.267
I'll give your wife a ride
in my Stingray.

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:41.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.267
Gonna have a lot of fun.

00:06:43.267 --> 00:06:44.667
[ Laughter ]
In fact, Biden really leaned

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:46.601
into economic populism
in his speech,

00:06:46.601 --> 00:06:48.801
tackling things the vast
majority of Americans hate,

00:06:48.801 --> 00:06:50.868
like absurdly high prices
for insulin,

00:06:50.868 --> 00:06:52.100
surprise medical bills,

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:54.100
high concert prices
jacked up by Ticketmaster,

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.467
[ Laughter ]
and junk fees
at banks and airlines.

00:06:56.467 --> 00:06:58.767
At one point, he even said
he wanted to eliminate

00:06:58.767 --> 00:07:00.534
surprise fees at hotels.

00:07:00.534 --> 00:07:02.400
-I know how unfair it feels

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.334
when a company overcharges you
and gets away with it.

00:07:05.334 --> 00:07:07.234
Not anymore.

00:07:07.234 --> 00:07:08.701
We've written a bill
to stop it all.

00:07:08.701 --> 00:07:12.000
It's called the Junk Fee
Prevention Act.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.634
We're going to ban surprise
resort fees

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:17.067
that hotels charge on your bill.

00:07:17.067 --> 00:07:19.133
Those fees can cost
up to $90 a night

00:07:19.133 --> 00:07:22.067
at hotels
that aren't even resorts.

00:07:22.067 --> 00:07:24.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:27.234 --> 00:07:30.000
I mean, you know

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.033
Joe Biden has stayed
at a Motel 6,

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:34.200
[ Laughter and applause ]
expecting better accommodation.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.901
[ As Biden ]
These aren't even
resorts, folks.

00:07:36.901 --> 00:07:37.767
[ Laughter ]

00:07:37.767 --> 00:07:39.834
No water slide, no golf course,

00:07:39.834 --> 00:07:42.067
and you got to pay
for the continental breakfast.

00:07:42.067 --> 00:07:43.901
[ Laughter ]
Plus, those metal chairs

00:07:43.901 --> 00:07:45.634
by the pool
give me waffle thighs.

00:07:45.634 --> 00:07:47.267
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.267 --> 00:07:49.467
And that focus on economic
populism is what led

00:07:49.467 --> 00:07:50.567
to the big moment of the night,

00:07:50.567 --> 00:07:52.334
when Biden
called out Republicans

00:07:52.334 --> 00:07:54.701
for proposing cuts
to Social Security and Medicare

00:07:54.701 --> 00:07:56.767
and threatening to hold
the country hostage

00:07:56.767 --> 00:07:58.834
over the debt ceiling,
unless Democrats acquiesce.

00:07:58.834 --> 00:08:00.334
It led to a lot
of Republican heckling,

00:08:00.334 --> 00:08:02.167
including that moment
we showed you earlier

00:08:02.167 --> 00:08:03.501
with Marjorie Taylor Greene.

00:08:03.501 --> 00:08:05.434
-Instead of making the wealthy
pay their fair share,

00:08:05.434 --> 00:08:07.067
some Republicans --

00:08:07.067 --> 00:08:10.567
some Republicans want Medicare
and Social Security to sunset.

00:08:10.567 --> 00:08:12.000
I'm not saying it's a majority.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.601
[ Booing ]

00:08:15.601 --> 00:08:17.467
Let me give you --

00:08:17.467 --> 00:08:19.601
Anybody who doubts it,

00:08:19.601 --> 00:08:21.234
contact my office.

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:23.133
I'll give you a copy.

00:08:23.133 --> 00:08:24.067
I'll give you a copy

00:08:24.067 --> 00:08:26.434
of the proposal.
-You're a liar!

00:08:26.434 --> 00:08:28.400
That means Congress
doesn't vote --

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.601
[ Shouting ]

00:08:29.601 --> 00:08:31.267
-Liar!
-I'm glad to see.

00:08:31.267 --> 00:08:32.968
I'm not saying
it's a majority of you.

00:08:32.968 --> 00:08:34.000
I don't even think it's even

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.501
a significant --
-Don't speak anymore.

00:08:35.501 --> 00:08:36.701
[ Shouting ]

00:08:36.701 --> 00:08:39.868
-But it's being proposed
by individuals.

00:08:39.868 --> 00:08:41.701
I'm politely not naming them,

00:08:41.701 --> 00:08:43.934
but it's being proposed
by some of you.

00:08:43.934 --> 00:08:44.901
-Okay, first of all,

00:08:44.901 --> 00:08:46.434
in a split screen
with these two,

00:08:46.434 --> 00:08:48.033
I'm definitely less inclined

00:08:48.033 --> 00:08:49.501
to believe the lady
who's dressed

00:08:49.501 --> 00:08:52.300
like she's leaving her entire
fortune to her cat.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.167
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.167 --> 00:08:54.400
"Oh, that's right,

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.334
you can all laugh at me now.

00:08:56.334 --> 00:08:58.000
Oh, laugh it on, Marjorie.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.767
But when I go, you get nothing,
nothing, you hear me?

00:09:00.767 --> 00:09:02.400
Mr. Poppenscotch,
on the other hand,

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:03.701
will live like a king!

00:09:03.701 --> 00:09:04.501
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.501 --> 00:09:05.868
Let's go, Mr. Poppenscotch.

00:09:05.868 --> 00:09:07.601
Why are you clawing at me,
you turncoat?

00:09:07.601 --> 00:09:08.734
Do you want to stay with them?

00:09:08.734 --> 00:09:10.701
Fine!
I'll just bury myself with it!"

00:09:10.701 --> 00:09:12.300
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:15.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:17.767 --> 00:09:20.868
[ Cheering ]

00:09:23.834 --> 00:09:26.367
[ Laughing ]

00:09:26.367 --> 00:09:29.033
Also, it's generally not
an effective tactic

00:09:29.033 --> 00:09:31.000
to debate the one guy
in the room

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.901
with a podium and a microphone,

00:09:32.901 --> 00:09:35.167
[ Laughter ]
especially when you have
to scream

00:09:35.167 --> 00:09:37.167
from the back row
without a microphone.

00:09:37.167 --> 00:09:38.567
That was like watching
a rap battle

00:09:38.567 --> 00:09:40.501
between Eminem and Shy Ronnie.

00:09:40.501 --> 00:09:41.868
[ Laughter ]
"SNL" classic.

00:09:41.868 --> 00:09:44.167
[ Vuvuzela blasts ]

00:09:44.167 --> 00:09:45.934
-♪ Speak up ♪

00:09:45.934 --> 00:09:47.300
-When you scream from the back,

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:49.200
you look like a crazy person
yelling at the bus driver

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:51.367
because he refused to drop you
off at the racetrack.

00:09:51.367 --> 00:09:52.534
[ Laughter ]

00:09:52.534 --> 00:09:54.000
And Greene isn't the only one

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.467
who made a big show
of disagreeing with Biden.

00:09:55.467 --> 00:09:57.067
There was also
Utah Senator Mike Lee,

00:09:57.067 --> 00:09:58.601
who pretended to be
utterly confused

00:09:58.601 --> 00:10:01.734
as to what Biden could possibly
be referring to when Biden said

00:10:01.734 --> 00:10:04.133
he would not allow the country
to default on its debt,

00:10:04.133 --> 00:10:06.634
if Republicans demanded cuts
to safety net programs.

00:10:06.634 --> 00:10:09.501
-We're not going to be moved
into being threatened

00:10:09.501 --> 00:10:12.033
to default on the debt,
if we don't respond.

00:10:12.033 --> 00:10:15.167
[ Cheering and applause ]
Folks.

00:10:15.167 --> 00:10:16.701
[ Laughter ]
-I'm sorry, are you
really confused,

00:10:16.701 --> 00:10:18.033
or are you just acting like

00:10:18.033 --> 00:10:19.968
you're in an episode
of "Curb Your Enthusiasm"?

00:10:19.968 --> 00:10:22.767
[ Laughter ]
"You said you would
cut Medicare, Larry!"

00:10:22.767 --> 00:10:24.033
[ As Larry ]
Ah...

00:10:24.033 --> 00:10:24.934
[ Laughter ]

00:10:24.934 --> 00:10:26.133
I don't think I did.

00:10:26.133 --> 00:10:27.467
"Yes, you did, Larry!"

00:10:27.467 --> 00:10:28.334
Not true, Rosie.

00:10:28.334 --> 00:10:30.334
"Yes, it is, you bald [bleep]!"

00:10:30.334 --> 00:10:31.000
And...

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:35.200
[ Laughter ]

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.234
...in Mike Lee's case,

00:10:36.234 --> 00:10:38.200
it would be true
because he campaigned

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:39.868
on eliminating Medicare
and Social Security

00:10:39.868 --> 00:10:42.033
when he first ran for Senate
back in 2010.

00:10:54.234 --> 00:10:54.901
-Nice!

00:10:56.501 --> 00:10:57.167
-Hear, hear.

00:10:57.167 --> 00:11:00.667
[ Applause ]

00:11:00.667 --> 00:11:02.367
-Um...
[ Tableware clunks, clinks ]

00:11:12.567 --> 00:11:13.234
-Sorry.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.734
-I mean, that's an insane thing
to admit on camera

00:11:16.734 --> 00:11:17.834
in American politics.

00:11:17.834 --> 00:11:18.968
Have you ever been
to a polling place?

00:11:18.968 --> 00:11:20.367
Half the people in there are
on their way

00:11:20.367 --> 00:11:22.133
to cash a Social Security check.

00:11:22.133 --> 00:11:23.667
[ Laughter ]
[ Oldster voice ]
I have two errands.

00:11:23.667 --> 00:11:25.167
I guess it's going to be
a nap day.

00:11:25.167 --> 00:11:27.200
[ Laughter ]
It's almost as bad
as complaining

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:29.267
about the price of salsa
for your crudité.

00:11:29.267 --> 00:11:31.601
[ Laughter ]
Here's my reaction
to finding out

00:11:31.601 --> 00:11:35.234
that Mike Lee called, on camera,
for eliminating Social Security.

00:11:36.634 --> 00:11:38.634
[ Laughter ]

00:11:38.634 --> 00:11:39.767
And he's not the only one.

00:11:39.767 --> 00:11:41.501
Senators Rick Scott
and Ron Johnson

00:11:41.501 --> 00:11:43.167
both floated plans
that would sunset

00:11:43.167 --> 00:11:44.934
Social Security and Medicare
by putting them

00:11:44.934 --> 00:11:47.400
up for periodic votes
that would subject them to cuts

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.167
and Georgia Republican
Congressman Rick Allen

00:11:49.167 --> 00:11:50.634
said he would raise
the retirement age

00:11:50.634 --> 00:11:52.968
because, he claims,
people come up to him

00:11:52.968 --> 00:11:54.934
and say they want
to work longer.

00:12:05.667 --> 00:12:07.167
-Mm-hmm?
-Yeah.

00:12:17.033 --> 00:12:18.934
-No, that's wrong.
If people want to work longer,

00:12:18.934 --> 00:12:20.334
you don't need to give them
an incentive

00:12:20.334 --> 00:12:21.968
because they already want
to do it.

00:12:21.968 --> 00:12:24.334
[ Laughter ]
You need incentives for things
people don't want to do,

00:12:24.334 --> 00:12:25.667
like [bleep] working longer

00:12:25.667 --> 00:12:28.167
[ Laughter ]
because you made that story up.

00:12:28.167 --> 00:12:29.400
As far as I can tell,
the only person

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:30.901
who actually wants
to work longer is Joe Biden.

00:12:30.901 --> 00:12:32.968
[ Laughter ]
Everyone thought that dude
would hang it up

00:12:32.968 --> 00:12:35.400
after he was vice president
at the age of 74,

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:36.868
but he watched Obama do it
and said,

00:12:36.868 --> 00:12:38.701
"Hey, I'd like to have
the world's hardest job

00:12:38.701 --> 00:12:40.100
and do it into my 80s.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:42.400
Plus, I hear they bring you
free balloons."

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.801
[ Laughter ]
And, honestly,

00:12:44.801 --> 00:12:47.067
who can blame Biden
for wanting to stick around,

00:12:47.067 --> 00:12:48.033
when these are his opponents?

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:49.467
Biden thrives when compared

00:12:49.467 --> 00:12:50.667
to the current era
of Republicans.

00:12:50.667 --> 00:12:51.667
Remember, Biden ran

00:12:51.667 --> 00:12:53.767
for president twice,
never got close.

00:12:53.767 --> 00:12:55.767
Ran against Trump, boom,
he's in the Oval Office.

00:12:55.767 --> 00:12:57.267
The beginning of his address
last night

00:12:57.267 --> 00:12:58.567
wasn't anything special,

00:12:58.567 --> 00:13:00.367
but then these lunatics
started heckling

00:13:00.367 --> 00:13:01.667
and you could see him
lick his lips

00:13:01.667 --> 00:13:05.000
and everyone thought, "Okay,
Grandpa came to play."

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:06.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:06.367 --> 00:13:09.100
These guys make Biden look like
a Harlem Globetrotter,

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:12.267
even though trotting
isn't exactly his strong suit.

00:13:12.267 --> 00:13:14.167
[ Laughter, ohhs, and applause ]

00:13:14.167 --> 00:13:15.901
If only he had Marjorie
Taylor Greene's balloon,

00:13:15.901 --> 00:13:17.634
he could've have just floated
up the stairs.

00:13:17.634 --> 00:13:19.534
[ Laughter, ohhs, and applause ]

00:13:19.534 --> 00:13:21.701
Biden could not have asked
for a better contrast

00:13:21.701 --> 00:13:23.000
than the one he got
last night --

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:24.834
a screaming lady
in a white fur coat

00:13:24.834 --> 00:13:27.133
and a party that straight-up
lied about his past support

00:13:27.133 --> 00:13:28.534
for cutting
or sunsetting programs

00:13:28.534 --> 00:13:30.400
that Americans
overwhelmingly support.

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:33.767
Biden rattled off applause lines
while McCarthy was stone-faced

00:13:33.767 --> 00:13:35.601
and Greene stomped her feet
so hard, it was...

00:13:35.601 --> 00:13:36.834
-Groundbreaking.

00:13:36.834 --> 00:13:39.000
[ Laughter ]
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:42.634
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

